{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:10.3390/molecules21121741","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":8,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"27999336","source":"MED","pmid":"27999336","pmcid":"PMC6273041","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC6273041"]},"doi":"10.3390/molecules21121741","title":"DeBouganin Diabody Fusion Protein Overcomes Drug Resistance to ADCs Comprised of Anti-Microtubule Agents.","authorString":"Chooniedass S, Dillon RL, Premsukh A, Hudson PJ, Adams GP, MacDonald GC, Cizeau J.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Chooniedass S","lastName":"Chooniedass","firstName":"Shilpa","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Viventia Bio Inc., Winnipeg, MB R3T 3Z1, Canada. SChooniedass@viventia.com."}]}},{"fullName":"Dillon RL","lastName":"Dillon","firstName":"Rachelle L","initials":"RL","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Viventia Bio Inc., Winnipeg, MB R3T 3Z1, Canada. RDillon@viventia.com."}]}},{"fullName":"Premsukh A","lastName":"Premsukh","firstName":"Arjune","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Viventia Bio Inc., Winnipeg, MB R3T 3Z1, Canada. APremsukh@Viventia.com."}]}},{"fullName":"Hudson PJ","lastName":"Hudson","firstName":"Peter J","initials":"PJ","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Avipep Pty Ltd., Parkville 3052, Victoria, Australia. Peter.Hudson@avipep.com.au."}]}},{"fullName":"Adams GP","lastName":"Adams","firstName":"Gregory P","initials":"GP","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4207-2881"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Eleven Biotherapeutics, Philadelphia, PA 19104, USA. GAdams@viventia.com."}]}},{"fullName":"MacDonald GC","lastName":"MacDonald","firstName":"Glen C","initials":"GC","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Eleven Biotherapeutics, Winnipeg, MB R3E 0W3, Canada. glen.macdonald@eleven.com."}]}},{"fullName":"Cizeau J","lastName":"Cizeau","firstName":"Jeannick","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Viventia Bio Inc., Winnipeg, MB R3T 3Z1, Canada. JCizeau@viventia.com."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4207-2881"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"12","volume":"21","journalIssueId":2500252,"dateOfPublication":"2016 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2016,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Molecules","title":"Molecules (Basel, Switzerland)","essn":"1420-3049","issn":"1420-3049","nlmid":"100964009","isoabbreviation":"Molecules"},"printPublicationDate":"2016-12-01"},"pubYear":"2016","pageInfo":"E1741","abstractText":"Antibody drug conjugates (ADC), comprised of highly potent small molecule payloads chemically conjugated to a full-length antibody, represent a growing class of therapeutic agents. The targeting of cytotoxic payloads via the specificity and selectivity of the antibody has led to substantial clinical benefits. However, ADC potency can be altered by mechanisms of resistance such as overexpression of efflux pumps or anti-apoptotic proteins. DeBouganin is a de-immunized variant of bouganin, a ribosome-inactivating protein (RIP) that blocks protein synthesis, thereby leading to apoptosis. When conjugated to trastuzumab (T-deB), deBouganin was more potent than ado-trastuzumab-emtansine (T-DM1) and unaffected by resistance mechanisms to which DM1 is susceptible. To further highlight the differentiating mechanism of action of deBouganin, HCC1419 and BT-474 tumor cells that survived T-DM1 or trastuzumab-MMAE (T-MMAE) treatment were treated with an anti-HER2 C6.5 diabody-deBouganin fusion protein or T-deB. C6.5 diabody-deBouganin and T-deB were potent against HCC1419 and BT-474 cells that were resistant to T-DM1 or T-MMAE killing. The resistant phenotype involved MDR pumps, Bcl-2 family members, and the presence of additional unknown pathways. Overall, the data suggest that deBouganin is effective against tumor cell resistance mechanisms selected in response to ADCs composed of anti-microtubule payloads.","affiliation":"Viventia Bio Inc., Winnipeg, MB R3T 3Z1, Canada. SChooniedass@viventia.com.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Line, Tumor"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Microtubules","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Escherichia coli"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Breast Neoplasms","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Intracellular Signaling Peptides and Proteins"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Carrier Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Membrane Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Recombinant Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"TO","qualifierName":"toxicity"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Antineoplastic Agents","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"TO","qualifierName":"toxicity"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},